From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:33:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fire the teleport events for passengers a teleported vehicle
 carries

The hook half of paper-patch 0035. One call in Entity#teleportAsync, placed
immediately after the root entity's own event hook and before the destination's
unload read lock is acquired.

That point has the four properties the call needs: the passenger tree is still
attached so the passengers can be enumerated, the vehicle has not moved so its
own from/to is what every node is about to be given, the root's event has
already had its chance to cancel, and no lock is held so a handler that throws
cannot leak one. It also sits above the same-region/cross-region branch, so one
hook covers same region, cross region and cross world.

See LophinyaPassengerTeleportEvents for the measured Paper baseline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
index 3cd2907a664d095c89e0a56c6981946e592610fd..69fb3335742d5d12e6e365077638e38b2e4a00ba 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
@@ -4597,6 +4597,14 @@ public abstract class Entity
         }
         // Lophinya end
 
+        // Lophinya start - the same events for the passengers this teleport carries along.
+        // The tree is still attached here and the vehicle has not moved, so the vehicle's own
+        // from/to is what every node is about to be moved to. Before the unload lock, so a handler
+        // that throws cannot leak it. See LophinyaPassengerTeleportEvents for the measured Paper
+        // baseline, including why a passenger's cancel is ignored.
+        fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaPassengerTeleportEvents.callForPassengers(this, destination, pos, yaw, pitch, cause);
+        // Lophinya end
+
         // Luminol start - Level hot unload apis
         if (!destination.levelUnloadStateLock.acquireRead()) {
             return false;
